{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "תנופה", :translit "tenufah", :gloss "waving"} {:he "וסמיך ליה", :translit "u-semikh leih", :gloss "and adjacent to it"} {:he "וישא ידיו", :translit "ve-yisa yadav", :gloss "and he raised his hands"} {:he "שהנושא כפיו צריך להניף בידיו", :translit "she-hanosei kapav tzarik lehanif be-yadav", :gloss "that the one who lifts his palms must perform tenufah with his hands"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking tenufah of 9:21 with lifting hands of 9:22 by verbal adjacency"}], :frame {:text "In the priestly investiture narrative, after the wave-offering Aaron lifts his hands toward the people and blesses them (Leviticus 9:22). Ba'al HaTurim reads the juxtaposition of tenufah (9:21) with the lifting of hands (9:22) as evidence that the lifting of hands in priestly blessing requires a waving motion.", :sources ["Leviticus 9:21" "Leviticus 9:22"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking tenufah of 9:21 with lifting hands of 9:22 by verbal adjacency", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:22.316285048Z", :model "glm-5.2"}